 ## Overview
-MSE Loss and PSNR Conversion computes the Mean Squared Error (MSE) between predicted and target RGB values (or volume voxels) to serve as the primary photometric loss for training neural volume rendering models, and converts this error into Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) for logging and evaluation [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It is distinguished from structural metrics like SSIM by treating all pixel errors equally and from geometric losses like Normal-L2 by operating directly on color intensity rather than surface normals [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
